        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.194,
            0.235,
            0.825,
            0.292
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Learning maths is not just about knowing some shortcuts and following procedures but about understanding ‘why’ something works."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.315,
            0.293,
            0.337
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.34,
            0.846,
            0.404
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find, without dividing, whether the following numbers are divisible by 9. (i) 123   (ii) 405   (iii) 8888   (iv) 93547   (v) 358095"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.412,
            0.673,
            0.433
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Find the smallest multiple of 9 with no odd digits."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.441,
            0.733,
            0.463
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Find the multiple of 9 that is closest to the number 6000."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.471,
            0.847,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. How many multiples of 9 are there between the numbers 4300 and 4400?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.531,
            0.522,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Shortcut for Divisibility by 3"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.563,
            0.848,
            0.638
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that all the multiples of 9 are also multiples of 3. That is, if a number is divisible by 9, it will also be divisible by 3. However, there are other multiples of 3 that are not multiples of 9 for example — 15, 33, and 87."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.648,
            0.848,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ The shortcut to find the divisibility by 3 is similar to the method for 9. A number is divisible by 3 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 3. Explore the remainders when powers of 10 are divided by 3. Explain why this method works."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.744,
            0.534,
            0.767
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Shortcut for Divisibility by 11"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.776,
            0.847,
            0.815
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Interestingly, the shortcut for 11 is also based on checking the remainders with place value. Let us see how."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
